From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Walter <christian.walter@9elements.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Oct 2025 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] board: aspeed: evb_ast2600: disable GPIO passthrough for
 turin2d24tm3-2l

Disable hardware GPIO passthrough by clearing SCU51C[9] during
board initialization to allow x86-power-control software passthrough
to function correctly.

Hardware passthrough locks GPIO pins making them uncontrollable by
software, preventing BMC power button control functionality.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded specific]

Signed-off-by: Christian Walter <christian.walter@9elements.com>
---
 board/aspeed/evb_ast2600/evb_ast2600.c | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/aspeed/evb_ast2600/evb_ast2600.c b/board/aspeed/evb_ast2600/evb_ast2600.c
index 1234567890..abcdef1234 100644
--- a/board/aspeed/evb_ast2600/evb_ast2600.c
+++ b/board/aspeed/evb_ast2600/evb_ast2600.c
@@ -131,3 +131,36 @@ int board_early_init_f(void)
 	espi_init();
 	return 0;
 }
+
+int board_late_init(void)
+{
+	u32 val_before, val_after;
+
+	printf("\n");
+	printf("========================================\n");
+	printf("ASRock Turin2D24TM3-2L Board Init\n");
+	printf("========================================\n");
+
+	/* Disable GPIO hardware passthrough (SCU51C[9])
+	 * This allows software control of power button GPIOs
+	 * via x86-power-control instead of hardware passthrough
+	 */
+	val_before = readl(SCU_BASE + 0x51C);
+	printf("SCU51C before: 0x%08x\n", val_before);
+
+	val_after = val_before & ~(1 << 9);  /* Clear bit 9 */
+	writel(val_after, SCU_BASE + 0x51C);
+
+	val_after = readl(SCU_BASE + 0x51C);
+	printf("SCU51C after:  0x%08x\n", val_after);
+
+	if (val_before & (1 << 9)) {
+		printf("GPIO hardware passthrough DISABLED\n");
+	} else {
+		printf("GPIO hardware passthrough was already disabled\n");
+	}
+	printf("========================================\n");
+	printf("\n");
+
+	return 0;
+}
